    "question": {
      ":question/id": "56d9e7ac-b7d2-5aa5-aac2-2f3da8fbf9a9",
      ":question/problem": "$\\int \\frac{2}{x+8}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let $u=x+8.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x+8}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x+8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x+8|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
